 338:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** /** @defgroup PWR_Group4 Main and Backup Regulators configuration functions
 339:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *  @brief   Main and Backup Regulators configuration functions 
 340:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *
 341:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** @verbatim   
 342:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================
 343:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           ##### Main and Backup Regulators configuration functions #####
 344:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 345:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****     [..]
 346:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) The backup domain includes 4 Kbytes of backup SRAM accessible only from 
 347:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           the CPU, and address in 32-bit, 16-bit or 8-bit mode. Its content is 
 348:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           retained even in Standby or VBAT mode when the low power backup regulator
 349:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           is enabled. It can be considered as an internal EEPROM when VBAT is 
 350:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           always present. You can use the PWR_BackupRegulatorCmd() function to 
 351:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           enable the low power backup regulator and use the PWR_GetFlagStatus
 352:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           (PWR_FLAG_BRR) to check if it is ready or not. 
 353:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** 
 354:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) When the backup domain is supplied by VDD (analog switch connected to VDD) 
 355:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           the backup SRAM is powered from VDD which replaces the VBAT power supply to 
 356:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           save battery life.
 357:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** 
 358:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) The backup SRAM is not mass erased by an tamper event. It is read 
 359:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           protected to prevent confidential data, such as cryptographic private 
 360:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           key, from being accessed. The backup SRAM can be erased only through 
 361:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           the Flash interface when a protection level change from level 1 to 
 362:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           level 0 is requested. 
 363:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       -@- Refer to the description of Read protection (RDP) in the reference manual.
 364:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** 
 365:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) The main internal regulator can be configured to have a tradeoff between 
 366:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           performance and power consumption when the device does not operate at 
 367:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           the maximum frequency. 
 368:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) For STM32F405xx/407xx and STM32F415xx/417xx  Devices, the regulator can be     
 369:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           configured on the fly through PWR_MainRegulatorModeConfig() function which  
 370:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           configure VOS bit in PWR_CR register:
 371:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) When this bit is set (Regulator voltage output Scale 1 mode selected) 
 372:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              the System frequency can go up to 168 MHz. 
 373:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) When this bit is reset (Regulator voltage output Scale 2 mode selected) 
 374:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              the System frequency can go up to 144 MHz.
 375:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              
 376:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****        (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx Devices, the regulator can be configured through    
 377:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            PWR_MainRegulatorModeConfig() function which configure VOS[1:0] bits in
 378:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            PWR_CR register:  
 379:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            which configure VOS[1:0] bits in PWR_CR register: 
 380:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) When VOS[1:0] = 11 (Regulator voltage output Scale 1 mode selected) 
 381:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              the System frequency can go up to 168 MHz. 
 382:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) When VOS[1:0] = 10 (Regulator voltage output Scale 2 mode selected) 
 383:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              the System frequency can go up to 144 MHz.  
 384:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) When VOS[1:0] = 01 (Regulator voltage output Scale 3 mode selected) 
 385:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              the System frequency can go up to 120 MHz. 
 386:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****                           
 387:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****        (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx Devices, the scale can be modified only when the PLL 
 388:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            is OFF and the HSI or HSE clock source is selected as system clock. 
 389:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            The new value programmed is active only when the PLL is ON.
 390:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            When the PLL is OFF, the voltage scale 3 is automatically selected. 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccqiEoki.s 			page 11


 391:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         Refer to the datasheets for more details.
 392:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         
 393:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****        (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx Devices, in Run mode: the main regulator has
 394:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            2 operating modes available:
 395:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) Normal mode: The CPU and core logic operate at maximum frequency at a given 
 396:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              voltage scaling (scale 1, scale 2 or scale 3)
 397:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) Over-drive mode: This mode allows the CPU and the core logic to operate at a 
 398:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****             higher frequency than the normal mode for a given voltage scaling (scale 1,  
 399:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****             scale 2 or scale 3). This mode is enabled through PWR_OverDriveCmd() function and
 400:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****             PWR_OverDriveSWCmd() function, to enter or exit from Over-drive mode please follow 
 401:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****             the sequence described in Reference manual.
 402:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              
 403:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****        (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx Devices, in Stop mode: the main regulator or low power regulator 
 404:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            supplies a low power voltage to the 1.2V domain, thus preserving the content of register
 405:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****            and internal SRAM. 2 operating modes are available:
 406:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****          (++) Normal mode: the 1.2V domain is preserved in nominal leakage mode. This mode is only 
 407:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****               available when the main regulator or the low power regulator is used in Scale 3 or 
 408:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****               low voltage mode.
 409:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****          (++) Under-drive mode: the 1.2V domain is preserved in reduced leakage mode. This mode is 
 410:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****               available when the main regulator or the low power regulator is in low voltage mode.
 411:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****               This mode is enabled through PWR_UnderDriveCmd() function.
 412:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****             
 413:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** @endverbatim
 414:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @{
 415:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   */
