 681:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** /** @defgroup PWR_Group6 Low Power modes configuration functions
 682:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *  @brief   Low Power modes configuration functions 
 683:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *
 684:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** @verbatim   
 685:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================
 686:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****               ##### Low Power modes configuration functions #####
 687:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 688:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****     [..]
 689:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       The devices feature 3 low-power modes:
 690:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Sleep mode: Cortex-M4 core stopped, peripherals kept running.
 691:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Stop mode: all clocks are stopped, regulator running, regulator 
 692:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           in low power mode
 693:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Standby mode: 1.2V domain powered off.
 694:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccqiEoki.s 			page 21


 695:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    *** Sleep mode ***
 696:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    ==================
 697:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****     [..]
 698:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 699:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) The Sleep mode is entered by using the __WFI() or __WFE() functions.
 700:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 701:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) Any peripheral interrupt acknowledged by the nested vectored interrupt 
 702:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              controller (NVIC) can wake up the device from Sleep mode.
 703:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** 
 704:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    *** Stop mode ***
 705:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    =================
 706:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****     [..]
 707:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       In Stop mode, all clocks in the 1.2V domain are stopped, the PLL, the HSI,
 708:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       and the HSE RC oscillators are disabled. Internal SRAM and register contents 
 709:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       are preserved.
 710:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       The voltage regulator can be configured either in normal or low-power mode.
 711:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       To minimize the consumption In Stop mode, FLASH can be powered off before 
 712:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       entering the Stop mode. It can be switched on again by software after exiting 
 713:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       the Stop mode using the PWR_FlashPowerDownCmd() function. 
 714:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    
 715:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 716:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) The Stop mode is entered using the PWR_EnterSTOPMode(PWR_MainRegulator_ON) 
 717:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              function with:
 718:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           (+++) Main regulator ON.
 719:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           (+++) Low Power regulator ON.
 720:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 721:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) Any EXTI Line (Internal or External) configured in Interrupt/Event mode.
 722:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       
 723:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    *** Standby mode ***
 724:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    ====================
 725:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****     [..]
 726:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       The Standby mode allows to achieve the lowest power consumption. It is based 
 727:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       on the Cortex-M4 deepsleep mode, with the voltage regulator disabled. 
 728:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       The 1.2V domain is consequently powered off. The PLL, the HSI oscillator and 
 729:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       the HSE oscillator are also switched off. SRAM and register contents are lost 
 730:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       except for the RTC registers, RTC backup registers, backup SRAM and Standby 
 731:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       circuitry.
 732:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    
 733:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       The voltage regulator is OFF.
 734:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       
 735:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 736:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) The Standby mode is entered using the PWR_EnterSTANDBYMode() function.
 737:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 738:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) WKUP pin rising edge, RTC alarm (Alarm A and Alarm B), RTC wakeup,
 739:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              tamper event, time-stamp event, external reset in NRST pin, IWDG reset.              
 740:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** 
 741:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    *** Auto-wakeup (AWU) from low-power mode ***
 742:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****    =============================================
 743:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****     [..]
 744:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       The MCU can be woken up from low-power mode by an RTC Alarm event, an RTC 
 745:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       Wakeup event, a tamper event, a time-stamp event, or a comparator event, 
 746:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       without depending on an external interrupt (Auto-wakeup mode).
 747:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** 
 748:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****       (#) RTC auto-wakeup (AWU) from the Stop mode
 749:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****        
 750:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) To wake up from the Stop mode with an RTC alarm event, it is necessary to:
 751:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           (+++) Configure the EXTI Line 17 to be sensitive to rising edges (Interrupt 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccqiEoki.s 			page 22


 752:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****                 or Event modes) using the EXTI_Init() function.
 753:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           (+++) Enable the RTC Alarm Interrupt using the RTC_ITConfig() function
 754:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           (+++) Configure the RTC to generate the RTC alarm using the RTC_SetAlarm() 
 755:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****                 and RTC_AlarmCmd() functions.
 756:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****         (++) To wake up from the Stop mode with an RTC Tamper or time stamp event, it 
 757:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****              is necessary to:
 758:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           (+++) Configure the EXTI Line 21 to be sensitive to rising edges (Interrupt 
 759:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****                 or Event modes) using the EXTI_Init() function.
 760:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****           (+++) Enable the RTC Tamper or time stamp Interrupt using the RTC_ITConfig() 
 761:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****                 function
