 852:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** /**
 853:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @brief  Enters in Under-Drive STOP mode.
 854:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *  
 855:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @note   This mode is only available for STM32F42xxx/STM3243xxx devices. 
 856:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * 
 857:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @note    This mode can be selected only when the Under-Drive is already active 
 858:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *         
 859:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @note   In Stop mode, all I/O pins keep the same state as in Run mode.
 860:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @note   When exiting Stop mode by issuing an interrupt or a wakeup event, 
 861:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *         the HSI RC oscillator is selected as system clock.
 862:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @note   When the voltage regulator operates in low power mode, an additional 
 863:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *         startup delay is incurred when waking up from Stop mode. 
 864:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *         By keeping the internal regulator ON during Stop mode, the consumption 
 865:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *         is higher although the startup time is reduced.
 866:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *     
 867:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @param  PWR_Regulator: specifies the regulator state in STOP mode.
 868:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *          This parameter can be one of the following values:
 869:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *            @arg PWR_MainRegulator_UnderDrive_ON:  Main Regulator in under-drive mode 
 870:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *                 and Flash memory in power-down when the device is in Stop under-drive mode
 871:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *            @arg PWR_LowPowerRegulator_UnderDrive_ON:  Low Power Regulator in under-drive mode 
 872:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *                and Flash memory in power-down when the device is in Stop under-drive mode
 873:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @param  PWR_STOPEntry: specifies if STOP mode in entered with WFI or WFE instruction.
 874:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *          This parameter can be one of the following values:
 875:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *            @arg PWR_STOPEntry_WFI: enter STOP mode with WFI instruction
 876:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   *            @arg PWR_STOPEntry_WFE: enter STOP mode with WFE instruction
 877:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   * @retval None
 878:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c ****   */
 879:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_pwr.c **** void PWR_EnterUnderDriveSTOPMode(uint32_t PWR_Regulator, uint8_t PWR_STOPEntry)
